<div class="mb-requirement-container">
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-14105">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> </span>
      <b>NOTE: </b> The official merit badge pamphlets are now free and
      downloadable
      <a
        href="https://filestore.scouting.org/filestore/Merit_Badge_ReqandRes/Pamphlets/Gardening.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        >HERE</a
      >
      or can be purchased at the
      <a href="https://www.scoutshop.org/" target="_blank ">Scout Shop.</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-13426">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 1. </span>
      Do the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13426 mb-requirement-id-13427">
        (a) Explain to your counselor the most likely hazards associated with
        gardening and what you should do to anticipate, help prevent, mitigate,
        and respond to these hazards. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/SgddPiUf61A" target="_blank"
          >Garden Safety Tips (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13426 mb-requirement-id-13428">
        (b) Discuss the prevention of and treatment for health concerns that
        could occur while gardening, including cuts, scratches, puncture wounds,
        insect bites, anaphylactic shock, heat reactions, and reactions from
        exposure to pesticides and fertilizers. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a
          href="https://youtu.be/fMidlx7VB0A?si=v5o_p4iwXa6Dxy8A"
          target="_blank"
          >Pesticide Safety (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-13413">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 2. </span>
      Do the following, and discuss your observations throughout the process
      with your counselor:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13413 mb-requirement-id-13414">
        (a) Grow six vegetables, three from seeds and three from seedlings,
        through harvest. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://youtube.com/shorts/7lZjUM__0lg" target="_blank"
          >How To Start Seeds at Home (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/BFhUmQyL4Bo" target="_blank"
          >How To Grow Cucumbers (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/RowLz52q8Og" target="_blank"
          >How To Grow Asparagus (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13413 mb-requirement-id-13415">
        (b) Grow six flowers, three from seeds and three from seedlings, through
        flowering. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/P82I3knYoqY" target="_blank"
          >How To Plant Flowers (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/Yv0MPxzFCvs" target="_blank"
          >How To Plant &amp; Grow Sunflowers (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-13416">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 3. </span>
      Give the nutritional value of the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13416 mb-requirement-id-13417">
        (a) Three root or tuber crops <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a
          href="https://youtu.be/0VjgXZBKfuQ?si=Uw0UYQkPgWfgqQfx"
          target="_blank"
          >Taro (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://youtu.be/o7ZwuSd8KRg?si=EEj5qNHCID4FDxYX"
          target="_blank"
          >Sweet Potatoes (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://youtu.be/3qCh8KZw_e0?si=f9aIa5z8f8LDDeLm"
          target="_blank"
          >Potatoes (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13416 mb-requirement-id-13418">
        (b) Three vegetables that bear above the ground <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/kzX-0rUbkOo" target="_blank"
          >Lettuce (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/M4T3bGDEyHY" target="_blank"
          >Tomato Health Benefits! (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/MVXr7HEMQMU" target="_blank"
          >Cucumbers (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13416 mb-requirement-id-13419">
        (c) Three fruits <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/SIDYB6e0Kxc" target="_blank"
          >Are Green Grapes Good for You? See 6 Reasons (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/0yEPKXlYQqQ" target="_blank">Apples (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/DkxhGscNC18&amp;t=1" target="_blank"
          >Oranges (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-13429">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 4. </span>
      Test 100 seeds for germination. Determine the percentage of seeds that
      germinate. Explain why you think some did not germinate. <br /><i
        >Resource:</i
      >
      <a href="https://youtu.be/E0jzPVGiKHs?si=6sRjzeuX1P0CgsSA" target="_blank"
        >Seed Germination Test (video)</a
      >
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-13430">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 5. </span>
      Visit your county extension office, local university, agricultural
      college, nursery, farm, botanical garden, or arboretum. Report on what you
      learned. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
      <a href="https://youtu.be/zMB6lTyXdnE" target="_blank"
        >Eyes on Agriculture (video)</a
      >
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-13431">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 6. </span>
      Explain to your counselor how and why honeybees are used in pollinating
      food crops and the problems that face the bee population today. Discuss
      what the impact to humanity would be if there were no pollinators.
      <br /><i>Resources:</i>
      <a href="https://youtu.be/Kdm9daKTRsc?si=I5GPFtrnBBb3RwPu" target="_blank"
        >All About Bees (video)</a
      ><br />
      <a href="https://youtu.be/Jzp6H8BAJ7o?si=GSLeo8yCvfJUS-4e" target="_blank"
        >Why Bees Are Important (video)</a
      >
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-13432">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 7. </span>
      Identify five garden pests (insects, diseased plants). Recommend two
      solutions for each pest. At least one of the two solutions must be an
      organic method. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
      <a href="https://youtu.be/6RcI869zno4" target="_blank"
        >Be a Bug Detective (video)</a
      ><br />
      <a href="https://youtu.be/K5hz_B0-LXc" target="_blank"
        >Good Bugs vs Bad Bugs: What's in Your Garden? (video)</a
      >
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-13420">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 8. </span>
      Do ONE of the following and record weekly observations. Discuss the
      results of your project with your counselor.
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13420 mb-requirement-id-13421">
        (a) Build a compost bin and maintain it for 90 days. <br /><i
          >Resource:</i
        >
        <a href="https://youtu.be/V2eKYvKgTOI" target="_blank"
          >Build a Compost Bin That Turns Yard Waste Into Soil (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13420 mb-requirement-id-13422">
        (b) Build a vermicompost bin (worm compost bin) and maintain it for 90
        days. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a
          href="https://youtu.be/C31jh3ohFwc?si=JaK1BOm1Zdj-9Cao"
          target="_blank"
          >How to Build a Worm Composter: A Simple DIY Vermicomposting Project
          (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13420 mb-requirement-id-13423">
        (c) Build a hydroponic garden containing three vegetables or herbs, or
        three ornamental plants. Maintain this garden through harvest or
        flowering, or for 90 days. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/LJuh6VGEfPc" target="_blank"
          >How To Grow an Indoor Hydroponic Garden (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/hBzrclNT4PI" target="_blank"
          >Hydroponics At Home (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13420 mb-requirement-id-13424">
        (d) Build one water garden, either in a container (at least 12 by 6
        inches and 6 inches deep), or in the ground as a small, decorative pond
        no larger than 6 by 3 feet and 24 inches deep. Maintain the water garden
        for 90 days. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a
          href="https://youtu.be/Y2ZL-9hRtLc?si=wxK-wWUh_DNaTdsX"
          target="_blank"
          >How to Create a Water Garden in a Pot (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13420 mb-requirement-id-13425">
        (e) Prepare a honey super for use on a hive or colony. Remove a filled
        honey super from the hive or colony and prepare the honey for sale.
        <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/q9jT2z0a5pA" target="_blank"
          >Adding a Second Super (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://blogs.ifas.ufl.edu/orangeco/2022/11/29/honey-harvesting-honey-out-of-the-hive"
          target="_blank"
          >Honey Harvesting: Honey out of the Hive (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13420 mb-requirement-id-13433">
        (f) Grow a garden of your own using soil from seed or plantings to
        harvest or for 90 days, whichever is earlier. This can be an outdoor
        garden or indoors using appropriate containers, and should include at
        least three types of plants approved by your counselor. <br /><i
          >Resources:</i
        >
        <a href="https://youtu.be/zpkz8ckO6Pc" target="_blank"
          >The Secret to a Garden That Produces All Summer Long (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/C6pvLVfEmKk" target="_blank"
          >How To Get Started Growing Organic Garden (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://youtu.be/dTsWMZIEr6M" target="_blank"
          >How To Have a Weed-Free Garden (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-13434">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 9. </span>
      Do ONE of the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13434 mb-requirement-id-13435">
        (a) Identify three career opportunities that would use skills and
        knowledge in gardening. Pick one and research the training, education,
        certification requirements, experience, and expenses associated with
        entering the field. Research the prospects for employment, starting
        salary, advancement opportunities and career goals associated with this
        career. Discuss what you learned with your counselor and whether you
        might be interested in this career. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a
          href="https://youtu.be/RVIvWuZ-TUk?si=Iyu26yzBvJHanASD"
          target="_blank"
          >Gardener - Career Spotlight (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.bls.gov/ooh/building-and-grounds-cleaning/grounds-maintenance-workers.htm"
          target="_blank"
          >Grounds Maintenance Workers (website w/ video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-13434 mb-requirement-id-13436">
        (b) Identify how you might use the skills and knowledge in gardening to
        pursue a personal hobby and/or healthy lifestyle. Research the
        additional training required, expenses, and affiliation with
        organizations that would help you maximize the enjoyment and benefit you
        might gain from it. Discuss what you learned with your counselor and
        share what short-term and long-term goals you might have if you pursued
        this. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a
          href="https://youtu.be/iVecXN-JQ64?si=Oi7akvlN2S3UerRT"
          target="_blank"
          >Benefits of Gardening as a Hobby and Why You Should Be a Gardener
          (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
</div>
